   329	## 4. Orevkov-excluded three-sheet negative control
   330	
   331	Orevkov's Theorem 1.1 states that a two- or three-sheeted polynomial map
   332	\(\mathbb C^2\to\mathbb C^2\) cannot have nonzero constant Jacobian. To ask
   333	whether action residues can see that theorem, use the unique \(\Lambda=3\)
   334	row-1 pole datum from Sigray's table, recorded in SHEET6-L1.md:
   335	
   336	\[
   337	 (D_F,D_g;\deg p,\deg p_g;\nu,M,\bar\kappa)
   338	 =(2,3;2,3;2,1,5).                                       \tag{4.1}
   339	\]
   340	
   341	Taking the same \(\kappa=42\) ramification as residue A makes
   342	\(\pi=37/42\) and realizes \(\bar\kappa=42(1-\pi)=5\). Put
   343	
   344	\[
   345	 x=t^{-42},\qquad y=\eta t^{37},
   346	\]
   347	
   348	\[
   349	 p=\eta^2-1,\qquad
   350	 q=14\eta\left(\eta^2-\frac32\right),
   351	\]
   352	
   353	\[
   354	 f=t^{-2}p,\qquad g=t^{-3}q.                              \tag{4.2}
   355	\]
   356	
   357	The pole ODE and both area forms agree exactly:
   358	
   359	\[
   360	 2pq'-3p'q=42,

