   361	 \qquad
   362	 dx\wedge dy=df\wedge dg=-42t^{-6}dt\wedge d\eta.        \tag{4.3}
   363	\]
   364	
   365	Even more strongly, this excluded-degree local datum has an explicit action
   366	primitive:
   367	
   368	\[
   369	 f\,dg-x\,dy
   370	 =d\!\left[
   371	 t^{-5}\frac{\eta(42\eta^4-105\eta^2+100)}5
   372	 \right].                                                \tag{4.4}
   373	\]
   374	
   375	Its action residue and its two fibre-action residues are all zero. If this were
   376	the sole pole of a global map, its \(\Lambda=3\) would give topological degree
   377	three, which Orevkov excludes. The calculation does **not** construct such a
   378	map; it proves that the action-residue test cannot detect the global obstruction.
   379	
   380	This is the decisive negative control. It is also structurally unsurprising:
   381	each residue-A pole \(P_i\) carries this same row-1 \(\Lambda=3\) pattern, and
   382	residue A gets \(td=3+3=6\) by using two of them. A placewise action residue
   383	cannot tell whether the global boundary contains one copy or two.
