   277	 \alpha\delta-\beta\gamma\ne0,
   278	\]
   279	
   280	then apply \((X,Y)\mapsto(X,Y-\phi(X))\), with
   281	\(\deg\phi=k\ge2\), and finally apply another invertible affine map. The
   282	last affine map cannot erase a highest-degree vector from both components,
   283	so it suffices to inspect \(X\).
