   652	
   653	## 6. The minimal remaining proof target
   654	
   655	KPC is deliberately scoped to *actual polynomial-origin packets*.  An
   656	equivalent operational statement is:
   657	
   658	> **CONJECTURE KPC (coefficient form).**  Let \(j\) be the first index for
   659	> which one of the divisibilities in (3.5) fails, or let a denominator order
   660	> be the first capacity failure.  For a packet produced by the exact eligible
   661	> Corollary-7.4 prefix of the selected polynomial Keller pair, no such first
   662	> failure exists.
   663	
   664	The separation family shows what a proof must rule out.  Its two weak
   665	numerators share the required boundary powers; their low transverse jets are
   666	tuned so that all nonmonomial terms in the cleared Jacobian cancel, leaving
   667	the allowed boundary monomial.  Therefore “take the first failed jet and read
   668	off a contradiction from \(df\wedge dg\)” is incomplete: the common
   669	reparametrization/contact-splitting alternative really occurs.
   670	
   671	There are two plausible sources of the missing contradiction.
   672	
   673	1. **Eligible-prefix saturation.**  A failed ordinary divisibility creates a
   674	   new Newton side after the selected root cut.  Prove that this side still
   675	   lies in the Corollary-7.4 eligible interval, or is the next certified cut,
   676	   and that its required common-power structure is incompatible with the
   677	   first failure.  This must be a theorem about the *entire prefix*, since
   678	   Proposition 5.1 shows that one face is insufficient.
   679	
   680	2. **Polynomial-origin/canonical-divisor compatibility.**  Use the exact
   681	   divisor of the pulled-back affine form \(dx\wedge dy\), not merely the fact
   682	   that its local coefficient is a monomial.  The valuations of the four
   683	   projective sections, the discrepancy coefficients, and the degree
   684	   identities \(d=B\alpha,e=B\beta\) may forbid the separation model on a
   685	   point lying in the polynomial pencil cluster.
   686	
   687	No theorem in the repository supplies either step.  FC5, the scalar depth
   688	invariant, NF-M, and the censuses forget precisely the transverse jets and
   689	canonical point ID needed here.  Accordingly KPC is labelled **CONJECTURE**.
   690	
   691	The strongest safe theorem is now:
   692	
   693	### Theorem 6.1 — exact WTC reduction (**PROVED**)
   694	
   695	For the selected polynomial pair and exact paired packets:
   696	
   697	\[
   698	 \boxed{\text{WTC-1}\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\text{KPC}.}      \tag{6.1}
   699	\]
