   772	## 8. The exact PCC remainder and an attempted proof
   773	
   774	### CONJECTURE PFE — packet-flag energy coverage
   775	
   776	For the selected polynomial Keller pair, the all-root occurrence forest is
   777	complete, every occurrence has the certified provenance required in §1, and
   778	the conservative point weights (7.2) satisfy
   779	
   780	\[
   781	 \boxed{\sum_pc_p^2\ge B^2-1.}                        \tag{PFE}
   782	\]
   783	
   784	KPC + PFE imply PCC term by term via (7.3), and hence imply
   785	\(\operatorname{td}\le\alpha\beta\).  PFE is the exact surviving content of
   786	the previous PCC-COVER after the point-identity/no-double-counting relation is
   787	made canonical.
   788	
   789	If the maximum convention is too strong, it can be replaced only by an
   790	explicit local packing function \(c_p^{\rm pack}\le h_p\), proved from
   791	pairwise-coprime ordinary initial factors.  Merely choosing unspecified
   792	\(c_p\le h_p\) with a large square sum is PCC itself and is circular.
   793	
   794	### 8.1 Contact splitting has the wrong quadratic sign
   795	
   796	Suppose, optimistically, that one packet of weight \(T\) has synchronized
   797	proportional contact vectors
   798	
   799	\[
   800	 R_{p_i}=\alpha u_i,qquad S_{p_i}=\beta u_i,qquad
   801	 \sum_i u_i=T.                                        \tag{8.1}
   802	\]
   803	
   804	Then its actual PCC mass is
   805	
   806	\[
   807	 \sum_i u_i^2
   808	 =T^2-2\sum_{i<j}u_i u_j\le T^2,                     \tag{8.2}
   809	\]
   810	
   811	with equality if and only if the packet is concentrated at one center.  Thus
   812	Noether contact conservation gives a *linear* identity, while PCC needs the
   813	opposite, maximally concentrated quadratic behavior.  Proximity by itself
   814	does not repair the sign; it records the splitting responsible for the loss.
   815	
   816	Proposition 5.1 is worse than synchronized splitting: the vectors \((1,1)\)
   817	and \((2,1)\) are not pointwise proportional, and the floor meet loses the
   818	entire unit packet.
   819	
   820	### 8.2 A sharp conditional obstruction to linear root enumeration
   821	
   822	Suppose an all-root theorem supplied positive integer weights
   823	\(T_1,\ldots,T_s\) with only the linear conservation law
   824	
   825	\[
   826	 \sum_iT_i=B.                                         \tag{8.3}
   827	\]
   828	
   829	If no weight equals \(B\), convexity gives
   830	
   831	\[
   832	 \sum_iT_i^2\le(B-1)^2+1
   833	 =B^2-2B+2<B^2-1\qquad(B\ge2).                        \tag{8.4}
   834	\]
   835	
   836	Hence enumerating all roots of a degree-\(B\) core and conserving their total
   837	multiplicity cannot prove PFE unless one root already carries all \(B\), or
   838	additional levels create certified mass not governed by (8.3).  This is why
   839	“all roots” is not yet a coverage theorem.
   840	
   841	### 8.3 What a proof of PFE must add
   842	
   843	The attempted proof stops at a precise place.  A successful argument needs a
   844	global telescope that simultaneously accounts for:
   845	
   846	1. creation of new packet weight at later eligible cuts;
   847	2. loss under repeated presentations, removed by Definition 7.1;
   848	3. loss under contact splitting, quantified by (8.2); and
   849	4. normalized divergence of the two pencil vectors, which can erase floors as
   850	   in Proposition 5.1.
   851	
   852	Equivalently, it needs to prove that all splitting and divergence defects
   853	leave at most one unit of residual point-basis energy:
   854	
   855	\[
   856	 B^2-\sum_pc_p^2\le1.                                 \tag{8.5}
   857	\]
   858	
   859	The GGV divisibility chain controls which powers may occur, but no banked
   860	identity relates its \(q_j,t_j\) to the quadratic defect in (8.5).  FC5 and the
   861	censuses provide scalar or frequency data after forgetting the point IDs and
   862	therefore cannot supply this telescope.  PFE remains **CONJECTURE**.
   863	
   864	A normalized multi-Rees/b-divisor approach may be better aligned with (8.5):
   865	the flag theorem already places packets on canonical Rees/valuation data, and
   866	one could seek an intersection inequality for the two entire cluster vectors
   867	instead of imposing KPC packet by packet.  That would bypass one-center
   868	concentration, but the required quadratic inequality is new and is not proved
   869	here.
