   463	## 4. Exact bookkeeping method
   464	
   465	The GL calculations used the power-sum basis and the Frobenius character
   466	formula. For \(\mu=(1^{m_1}2^{m_2}\cdots)\), put
   467	\(z_\mu=\prod_i i^{m_i}m_i!\). The script formed
   468	
   469	\[
   470	h_r[h_m]
   471	=\sum_{\nu\vdash r}\frac1{z_\nu}
   472	\prod_{k\in\nu}
   473	\left(\sum_{\rho\vdash m}\frac{p_{k\rho}}{z_\rho}\right)
   474	\]
   475	
   476	as an exact partition-to-Fraction dictionary. It recovered Schur
   477	multiplicities by
   478	
   479	\[
   480	[S_\lambda]f=\sum_\mu[p_\mu]f\,\chi^\lambda(\mu).
   481	\]
   482	
   483	The integer characters were computed independently from the Frobenius
   484	coefficient formula
   485	
   486	\[
   487	\chi^\lambda(\mu)
   488	=[x^{\lambda+\delta}]\,\Delta(x)p_\mu(x),
   489	\qquad \delta=(n-1,n-2,\ldots,0),
   490	\]
   491	
   492	by enumerating the at most \(4!\) Vandermonde monomials and assigning the
   493	parts of \(\mu\) to four variables. Pieri was then an exact horizontal-strip
   494	test. Internal checks included the \(S_3\) standard character row
   495	\((2,0,-1)\), Weyl-dimension sums, and the independent GL2 checks
   496	
   497	\[
   498	\dim S_{(2,1)}(\mathbb C^5)=40,\qquad
   499	\dim S_{(2,2)}(\mathbb C^5)=50.
   500	\]
   501	
   502	No numerical character evaluation or interpolation enters the result.
   503	
