   261	## 4. T4 — Jelonek asymptotic variety
   262	
   263	VERDICT: **PASS (consistent), with exact geometric degree mu(F) = 6 and
   264	a quantified non-properness excess >= 6.**
   265	
   266	Criteria:
   267	- (J-1) [Jelonek, Ann. Polon. Math. 58 (1993)] For a dominant polynomial
   268	  F = (f,g): C^2 -> C^2 the non-properness set A(F) is empty or a curve;
   269	  every irreducible component is the image of a polynomial map C -> C^2
   270	  (hence a rational curve with ONE place at infinity). A Keller
   271	  counterexample is non-proper (a proper Keller map is invertible), so
   272	  A(F) is a nonempty curve.
   273	- (J-2) [Jelonek, degree bound; Testing sets for properness, 1999-2002]
   274	  deg A(F) <= (deg f * deg g - mu(F)) / min(deg f, deg g), mu(F) =
   275	  geometric degree. (Bound form quoted from memory; only used as a
   276	  sanity ceiling, nothing below depends on its exact shape.)
   277	
